---
description: Tenant queries use authorized_scope, not current_organization associations
alwaysApply: true
---

# Action Policy tenant scoping

Organization-owned records are scoped through Action Policy `relation_scope`, not `current_organization` associations in controllers.

```ruby
# bad
@customers = current_organization.customers.order(:company)
@customer = current_organization.customers.find(params[:id])
```

```ruby
# good
@customers = authorized_scope(Customer.all).order(:company)
@customer = authorized_scope(Customer.all).find(params[:id])
```

Put the filter on `OrganizationOwnedPolicy` via `relation_scope` (for example `relation.in_org(organization)`). Controllers then chain `order` / `includes` / `find` / `count` / `limit` on `authorized_scope(Model.all)`.

Keep `current_organization` for the sidebar name, org switcher, and `ApplicationController#current_organization`. `CurrentOrganizationsController` still uses `current_user.organizations` for membership switching.

Do not put `organization_id` on `User` or `Session`. Do not add `verify_authorized` globally.
